      "hints": [
        "Number density is the total number of free electrons divided by the wire volume.",
        "Use cross-sectional area multiplied by length for the wire volume."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "The wire volume is AL = (1.5 × 10⁻⁶)(1.8) m³.",
        "Number density n = N / (AL) = (2.3 × 10²³) / [(1.5 × 10⁻⁶)(1.8)].",
        "This gives n = 8.5 × 10²⁸ m⁻³."
